{"format":"bench-library","formatVersion":1,"id":"climate-sensors","name":"Climate sensors","version":"1.0.0","author":"Bench Workshop","owner":"codeopen0-cpu","description":"Temperature and humidity: the DHT11 and DHT22 (one data wire) and the BME280 (I2C, with air pressure). Set the weather with sliders in the run panel. Includes DHT.h and Adafruit_BME280.h.","category":"Sensors","needsApp":"0.3.0","code":"// Climate sensors. The DHTs talk on one wire: the board pulls it low to ask, and the sensor answers\n// with 40 bits (humidity, temperature, a checksum). Here the ask and the answer are messages on that\n// wire ('data'); the bytes are the real ones. The BME280 answers on I2C.\n\n/** a DHT's 5-byte answer */\nfunction dhtFrame(type, t, h) {\n  let b;\n  if (type === 11) {\n    const ti = Math.round(Math.max(0, Math.min(50, t))), hi = Math.round(Math.max(20, Math.min(90, h)));\n    b = [hi, 0, ti, 0];\n  } else {\n    const hv = Math.round(Math.max(0, Math.min(100, h)) * 10);\n    const tv = Math.round(Math.abs(Math.max(-40, Math.min(80, t))) * 10);\n    b = [hv >> 8, hv & 255, ((tv >> 8) & 0x7f) | (t < 0 ? 0x80 : 0), tv & 255];\n  }\n  return [...b, (b[0] + b[1] + b[2] + b[3]) & 255];\n}\n\nconst dht = (type) => (part) => {\n  const temp = part.control('temp'), hum = part.control('hum');\n  let powered = false, asked = 0, answered = 0, wantAnswer = false, lastAsk = -10, tooSoon = 0;\n  return {\n    packets(list) {\n      for (const p of list) if (p.pin === 'DATA' && p.proto === 'data' && p.data[0] === 1) wantAnswer = true;\n    },\n    step(io) {\n      const v = io.supply('VCC', 'GND');\n      powered = v >= 3;\n      if (powered) io.drive('DATA', v, 0); // (the module's pull-up)\n      else io.release('DATA');\n      if (wantAnswer) {\n        wantAnswer = false;\n        asked++;\n        // read more often than it can measure: a real one gives its last reading (or nothing)\n        if (io.time - lastAsk < (type === 11 ? 1 : 2)) tooSoon++;\n        lastAsk = io.time;\n        if (powered) {\n          io.send('DATA', 'data', dhtFrame(type, temp.value, hum.value));\n          answered++;\n        }\n      }\n      io.draw(powered ? (asked ? 0.0015 : 0.00005) : 0);\n    },\n    status() {\n      if (!powered) return ['no power (VCC needs 3.3-5 V)'];\n      return [`${temp.value.toFixed(type === 11 ? 0 : 1)} C, ${hum.value.toFixed(type === 11 ? 0 : 1)} %`, `asked ${asked} times${tooSoon ? ` (${tooSoon} too soon after the last)` : ''}`];\n    },\n  };\n};\nbench.device('dht11', dht(11));\nbench.device('dht22', dht(22));\n\n// BME280 (simplified registers, as the included Adafruit_BME280.h reads them):\n//   0xD0 chip id = 0x60; 0xF7-0xF9 pressure (Pa, 24 bits); 0xFA-0xFB temperature (hundredths of\n//   a degree, signed 16 bits); 0xFC-0xFD humidity (hundredths of a percent)\nbench.device('bme280', (part) => {\n  const temp = part.control('temp'), hum = part.control('hum'), pres = part.control('pres');\n  const addr = Number(part.params.addr ?? 0x76);\n  let powered = false, reg = 0, reads = 0;\n  const regs = () => {\n    const r = new Array(256).fill(0);\n    r[0xd0] = 0x60;\n    const p = Math.round(pres.value * 100), t = Math.round(temp.value * 100) & 0xffff, h = Math.round(hum.value * 100);\n    r[0xf7] = (p >> 16) & 255; r[0xf8] = (p >> 8) & 255; r[0xf9] = p & 255;\n    r[0xfa] = t >> 8; r[0xfb] = t & 255;\n    r[0xfc] = h >> 8; r[0xfd] = h & 255;\n    return r;\n  };\n  return {\n    i2c: {\n      address: () => (powered ? addr : -1),\n      write(bytes) { if (bytes.length) reg = bytes[0]; return true; },\n      read(n) {\n        reads++;\n        const r = regs();\n        const out = [];\n        for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) out.push(r[(reg + i) & 255]);\n        return out;\n      },\n    },\n    step(io) {\n      powered = io.supply('VIN', 'GND') >= 1.7;\n      io.draw(powered ? 0.0004 : 0);\n    },\n    status() {\n      if (!powered) return ['no power'];\n      return [`${temp.value.toFixed(1)} C, ${hum.value.toFixed(1)} %, ${pres.value.toFixed(1)} hPa`, `I2C 0x${addr.toString(16)}, ${reads} reads`];\n    },\n  };\n});\n","sketch":{"DHT.h":{"classes":["DHT"],"exports":["DHT11","DHT12","DHT21","DHT22","AM2301"],"code":"// DHT.h (Adafruit's DHT sensor library): DHT dht(pin, DHT22); dht.begin(); readTemperature(),\n// readHumidity(), computeHeatIndex(), convertCtoF(). Like the real one it reads the sensor at most\n// every 2 s (giving the last reading in between) and gives NAN when the sensor doesn't answer.\nconst DHT11 = 11, DHT12 = 12, DHT21 = 21, DHT22 = 22, AM2301 = 21;\n\nclass DHT {\n  constructor(pin, type = DHT22) {\n    this.pin = pin;\n    this.type = type;\n    this.last = -1e9;\n    this.ok = false;\n    this.data = [0, 0, 0, 0, 0];\n  }\n  begin() {\n    pinMode(this.pin, INPUT_PULLUP);\n    this.last = millis() - 2000;\n  }\n  /** ask the sensor (the board pulls the wire low, then listens): true if it answered */\n  read(force = false) {\n    if (!force && millis() - this.last < 2000) return this.ok;\n    this.last = millis();\n    linkReceive(this.pin, 'data'); // (anything old on the wire)\n    linkSend(this.pin, 'data', [1, this.type]);\n    const until = millis() + 40;\n    while (millis() < until) {\n      const got = linkReceive(this.pin, 'data');\n      if (got.length) {\n        const d = got[got.length - 1].data;\n        this.ok = d.length === 5 && ((d[0] + d[1] + d[2] + d[3]) & 255) === d[4];\n        if (this.ok) this.data = d;\n        return this.ok;\n      }\n      delay(1);\n    }\n    this.ok = false; // nobody answered: is it wired, and powered?\n    return false;\n  }\n  readTemperature(fahrenheit = false, force = false) {\n    if (!this.read(force)) return NAN;\n    const d = this.data;\n    let t;\n    if (this.type === DHT11 || this.type === DHT12) t = d[2] + (d[3] & 0x0f) * 0.1;\n    else {\n      t = (((d[2] & 0x7f) << 8) | d[3]) * 0.1;\n      if (d[2] & 0x80) t = -t;\n    }\n    return fahrenheit ? this.convertCtoF(t) : t;\n  }\n  readHumidity(force = false) {\n    if (!this.read(force)) return NAN;\n    const d = this.data;\n    if (this.type === DHT11 || this.type === DHT12) return d[0] + d[1] * 0.1;\n    return ((d[0] << 8) | d[1]) * 0.1;\n  }\n  convertCtoF(c) { return c * 1.8 + 32; }\n  convertFtoC(f) { return (f - 32) * 0.55555; }\n  /** how hot it feels (NOAA's formula, as the real library) */\n  computeHeatIndex(t, h, fahrenheit = true) {\n    const T = fahrenheit ? t : this.convertCtoF(t);\n    let hi = 0.5 * (T + 61.0 + (T - 68.0) * 1.2 + h * 0.094);\n    if (hi > 79) {\n      hi = -42.379 + 2.04901523 * T + 10.14333127 * h - 0.22475541 * T * h - 0.00683783 * T * T - 0.05481717 * h * h + 0.00122874 * T * T * h + 0.00085282 * T * h * h - 0.00000199 * T * T * h * h;\n      if (h < 13 && T >= 80 && T <= 112) hi -= ((13 - h) * 0.25) * Math.sqrt((17 - Math.abs(T - 95)) * 0.05882);\n      else if (h > 85 && T >= 80 && T <= 87) hi += ((h - 85) * 0.1) * ((87 - T) * 0.2);\n    }\n    return fahrenheit ? hi : this.convertFtoC(hi);\n  }\n}\n"},"Adafruit_BME280.h":{"classes":["Adafruit_BME280"],"code":"// Adafruit_BME280.h, the usual parts: begin(address), readTemperature(), readHumidity(),\n// readPressure() (Pa), readAltitude(seaLevel hPa), sensorID(). (This sensor's registers are\n// simplified in Bench Workshop: see the part's description.)\nclass Adafruit_BME280 {\n  constructor() { this.addr = 0x77; }\n  begin(addr = 0x77) {\n    this.addr = addr;\n    Wire.begin();\n    const id = this.reg(0xd0, 1);\n    return !!id && id[0] === 0x60;\n  }\n  sensorID() { const id = this.reg(0xd0, 1); return id ? id[0] : 0; }\n  reg(r, n) {\n    Wire.beginTransmission(this.addr);\n    Wire.write(r);\n    if (Wire.endTransmission() !== 0) return null;\n    if (Wire.requestFrom(this.addr, n) !== n) return null;\n    const out = [];\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) out.push(Wire.read());\n    return out;\n  }\n  readTemperature() {\n    const d = this.reg(0xfa, 2);\n    if (!d) return NAN;\n    let t = (d[0] << 8) | d[1];\n    if (t & 0x8000) t -= 0x10000;\n    return t / 100;\n  }\n  readHumidity() {\n    const d = this.reg(0xfc, 2);\n    return d ? ((d[0] << 8) | d[1]) / 100 : NAN;\n  }\n  readPressure() {\n    const d = this.reg(0xf7, 3);\n    return d ? (d[0] << 16) | (d[1] << 8) | d[2] : NAN; // (Pa)\n  }\n  /** metres above where the pressure would be seaLevel hPa */\n  readAltitude(seaLevel = 1013.25) {\n    const p = this.readPressure() / 100;\n    return 44330 * (1 - Math.pow(p / seaLevel, 0.1903));\n  }\n  seaLevelForAltitude(altitude, pressure) { return pressure / Math.pow(1 - altitude / 44330, 5.255); }\n  setSampling() {}\n  takeForcedMeasurement() { return true; }\n}\n"}},"parts":[{"id":"dht11","name":"DHT11 (temperature, humidity)","description":"The blue one: 0-50 C (whole degrees), 20-90 % humidity. VCC (3.3-5 V), DATA to a pin (the module has its pull-up), GND. Read it at most once a second. DHT dht(PIN, DHT11);","swatch":"#2f7fd8","mass":3,"shape":[{"box":[1.6,0.16,2.6],"at":[0,0.08,0],"color":"#1d6b3a"},{"box":[1.2,0.55,1.55],"at":[0,0.435,0.3],"color":"#2f7fd8"},{"box":[1,0.02,1.2],"at":[0,0.72,0.3],"color":"#5fa3ec","collide":false}],"pins":[{"id":"VCC","label":"VCC (3.3-5.5 V)","at":[-0.254,0.16,-1.1],"kind":"vin","vmin":3,"vmax":5.5},{"id":"DATA","at":[0,0.16,-1.1],"kind":"out","pulled":"up"},{"id":"GND","at":[0.254,0.16,-1.1],"kind":"gnd"}],"controls":[{"id":"temp","kind":"slider","label":"Temperature (C)","min":0,"max":50,"step":1,"value":22},{"id":"hum","kind":"slider","label":"Humidity (%)","min":20,"max":90,"step":1,"value":45}],"device":"dht11"},{"id":"dht22","name":"DHT22 (temperature, humidity)","description":"The white one: -40-80 C and 0-100 % in tenths. VCC (3.3-5 V), DATA to a pin (the module has its pull-up), GND. Read it at most every 2 seconds. DHT dht(PIN, DHT22);","swatch":"#f2f2f2","mass":4,"shape":[{"box":[1.6,0.16,3],"at":[0,0.08,0],"color":"#1d6b3a"},{"box":[1.5,0.75,2],"at":[0,0.535,0.4],"color":"#f2f2f2"},{"box":[1.3,0.02,1.5],"at":[0,0.92,0.4],"color":"#d6d6d6","collide":false}],"pins":[{"id":"VCC","label":"VCC (3.3-5.5 V)","at":[-0.254,0.16,-1.3],"kind":"vin","vmin":3,"vmax":5.5},{"id":"DATA","at":[0,0.16,-1.3],"kind":"out","pulled":"up"},{"id":"GND","at":[0.254,0.16,-1.3],"kind":"gnd"}],"controls":[{"id":"temp","kind":"slider","label":"Temperature (C)","min":-40,"max":80,"step":0.1,"value":22.5},{"id":"hum","kind":"slider","label":"Humidity (%)","min":0,"max":100,"step":0.1,"value":45}],"device":"dht22"},{"id":"bme280","name":"BME280 (temperature, humidity, pressure)","description":"A tiny I2C sensor (address 0x76, or 0x77 with its jumper). VIN (3.3-5 V), GND, SCL, SDA. Adafruit_BME280 bme; bme.begin(0x76); then readTemperature(), readHumidity(), readPressure() (Pa), readAltitude(1013.25). Its registers are simplified here: use the included Adafruit_BME280.h.","swatch":"#7a3ec8","mass":2,"params":[{"key":"addr","label":"I2C address","kind":"select","options":[{"value":"118","label":"0x76"},{"value":"119","label":"0x77"}]}],"defaults":{"addr":"118"},"shape":[{"box":[1.3,0.16,1.5],"at":[0,0.08,0],"color":"#7a3ec8"},{"box":[0.25,0.1,0.25],"at":[0,0.21,0.3],"color":"#c9cdd4"}],"pinRows":[{"ids":["VIN","GND","SCL","SDA"],"at":[-0.381,0,-0.6],"kinds":{"VIN":"vin","GND":"gnd","SCL":"i2c","SDA":"i2c"},"extra":{"VIN":{"label":"VIN (3.3-5 V)","vmin":1.7,"vmax":5.5}}}],"controls":[{"id":"temp","kind":"slider","label":"Temperature (C)","min":-40,"max":85,"step":0.1,"value":21},{"id":"hum","kind":"slider","label":"Humidity (%)","min":0,"max":100,"step":0.5,"value":50},{"id":"pres","kind":"slider","label":"Air pressure (hPa)","min":850,"max":1085,"step":0.5,"value":1013.25}],"device":"bme280"}],"examples":[{"name":"Weather to serial (DHT22)","description":"A DHT22 read every 2 seconds: temperature, humidity and the heat index in the serial monitor. Move its sliders in the run panel.","project":{"format":"bench-workshop","version":1,"name":"Weather to serial (DHT22)","parts":[{"uid":"board","type":"maker-board","name":"Board","params":{"usb":true},"parent":null,"pos":[-5,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"dht","type":"climate-sensors/dht22","name":"DHT22","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[4,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]}],"wires":[{"id":"w1","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"3V3"},"b":{"uid":"dht","pin":"VCC"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w2","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP2"},"b":{"uid":"dht","pin":"DATA"},"color":"#e8c547"},{"id":"w3","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND"},"b":{"uid":"dht","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"}],"programs":{"board":{"lang":"arduino","source":"// Temperature and humidity from a DHT22. Move its sliders in the run panel.\n#include <DHT.h>\n\n#define DHTPIN 2\n#define DHTTYPE DHT22\n\nDHT dht(DHTPIN, DHTTYPE);\n\nvoid setup() {\n  Serial.begin(115200);\n  dht.begin();\n}\n\nvoid loop() {\n  delay(2000);   // a DHT22 measures every 2 seconds at most\n  float h = dht.readHumidity();\n  float t = dht.readTemperature();\n  if (isnan(h) || isnan(t)) {\n    Serial.println(\"No answer from the DHT22: check its wires\");\n    return;\n  }\n  float feels = dht.computeHeatIndex(t, h, false);\n  Serial.print(\"Humidity: \");\n  Serial.print(h, 1);\n  Serial.print(\" %  Temperature: \");\n  Serial.print(t, 1);\n  Serial.print(\" C  Feels like: \");\n  Serial.print(feels, 1);\n  Serial.println(\" C\");\n}\n"}},"boards":[]}},{"name":"Weather to serial (BME280)","description":"A BME280 on I2C: temperature, humidity, pressure and altitude every second. Move its sliders in the run panel.","project":{"format":"bench-workshop","version":1,"name":"Weather to serial (BME280)","parts":[{"uid":"board","type":"maker-board","name":"Board","params":{"usb":true},"parent":null,"pos":[-5,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"bme","type":"climate-sensors/bme280","name":"BME280","params":{"addr":"118"},"parent":null,"pos":[4,0,2],"rot":[0,0,0,1]}],"wires":[{"id":"w1","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"3V3"},"b":{"uid":"bme","pin":"VIN"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w2","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND"},"b":{"uid":"bme","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w3","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"SDA"},"b":{"uid":"bme","pin":"SDA"},"color":"#4f9cff"},{"id":"w4","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"SCL"},"b":{"uid":"bme","pin":"SCL"},"color":"#e8c547"}],"programs":{"board":{"lang":"arduino","source":"// Temperature, humidity, air pressure and altitude from a BME280 (I2C, address 0x76).\n#include <Wire.h>\n#include <Adafruit_BME280.h>\n\nAdafruit_BME280 bme;\n\nvoid setup() {\n  Serial.begin(115200);\n  if (!bme.begin(0x76)) {\n    Serial.println(\"No BME280 at 0x76: check the wires (or try 0x77)\");\n    while (1) delay(1000);\n  }\n}\n\nvoid loop() {\n  Serial.print(bme.readTemperature(), 1);\n  Serial.print(\" C  \");\n  Serial.print(bme.readHumidity(), 1);\n  Serial.print(\" %  \");\n  Serial.print(bme.readPressure() / 100.0, 1);\n  Serial.print(\" hPa  about \");\n  Serial.print(bme.readAltitude(1013.25), 0);\n  Serial.println(\" m up\");\n  delay(1000);\n}\n"}},"boards":[]}}]}